or:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">Valerie, Novaya Ga=
zeta, the last big independent Russian media organization, closed its newsr=
oom this week. The paper and its journalists have been under intense pressu=
re from President Vladimir Putin for decades. Why now=3F</span></p><p style=
=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>T=
he real miracle is that they lasted this long. We=E2=80=99ve watched the Ru=
ssian government systematically dismantle any media organization that is cr=
itical of the Kremlin and critical of the war in Ukraine. This didn=E2=80=
=99t happen overnight.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,=
serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>First their website was blocked, so=
 you needed a VPN to read them. Then they lost their media license. Then Pu=
tin signed a decree nationalizing their printing presses. Then this spring,=
 authorities </span><a href=3D"https://nl.nytimes.com/f/newsletter/b64N8FtD=
