dwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:underline;text-decora=
tion:underline">raided the newsroom</a><span> and one of their journalists =
was detained and put on trial. The paper was added to the list of so-called=
 foreign agents =E2=80=94 this kind of Stalin-era term that comes with many=
 limitations on what you=E2=80=99re allowed to do.</span></p><p style=3D"fo=
nt:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>There w=
as this idea that eventually they would give up, but they didn=E2=80=99t. W=
hat ultimately forced them to close was when their landlord refused to rene=
w their lease after 20 years and their bank stopped processing the reader d=
onations that were their only remaining source of revenue. They went to oth=
er banks saying, Will you help us=3F But everyone said no. And that=E2=80=
=99s a function of either direct pressure from the authorities, or the unde=
rstanding that you=E2=80=99re going to have a problem if you keep working w=
ith the paper.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;co=
lor:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>And so they made the decision that they cou=
